Localized corrective revision of this exact Hearthmere civic-spring-spine draft. Preserve the existing camera, landscape framing, cold rainy lighting, wet-slate and repaired-dark-timber material treatment, one dominant open timber civic bell tower at left, one open public square, one stone spring-channel arch at right, spring channel, roofs, palisade, market awning, ledger desk, clay-name rack, banked brazier, rain chains, barrels, benches, architecture, scale, and grounded stylized 3D dark-fantasy finish as closely as possible. Make only the following hard corrections.

1. EXACTLY ONE BELFRY/TOWER TOTAL. Completely remove the pointed louvered cupola/belfry from the ridge of the large rear building at upper center-right. Replace it with an uninterrupted ordinary steep slate roof ridge in the same material and weather. Add no replacement turret, vent tower, spire, lantern, steeple, dormer shaped like a belfry, or distant tower. The existing large open timber bell tower at left is the only belfry or tower silhouette anywhere in the image.

2. EXACTLY EIGHT HUMAN RESIDENTS TOTAL in the entire image, counting foreground, midground, distant, doorway, window, tower-interior, and silhouette figures. Retain or clearly show exactly these eight noncombat workers and nobody else:
- one basket carrier at the left foreground doorway;
- one foreground walker on the broad public route;
- one seated or leaning ledger clerk at the public work desk;
- one water-and-handcart worker on the right spring service route;
- exactly three ordinary residents together in the middle distance of the square;
- one market repair or herb worker beneath the oxblood awning.
Remove every other human or human-shaped figure, especially all people on the left stair, at the right wall/door, behind counters, inside or beneath the bell tower, in doorways or windows, and in the far background. Leave cleared working space where removed; do not replace them with statues, dummies, effigies, creatures, or person-shaped props.

3. MAKE THE THIRD ROUTE RECONNECT IN FRAME. Preserve the broad foreground wet-slate public route and the narrower right spring-side handcart service route. Rework the current left stair/threshold circulation into a clearly traceable narrow return/shortcut lane: it must leave the rear-left edge of the square, travel visibly along the left inhabited thresholds beneath the eaves, descend on the left, and physically rejoin the foreground public route inside the lower-left-to-lower-center portion of the frame. Show continuous walkable paving and the actual junction. It must not disappear behind a building, dead-end, become an isolated stair, or require arrows/lines/signage. Keep exactly these three route roles.

4. MAKE THREE WORKING ARTIFACTS UNMISTAKABLE without adding clutter or text:
- one small chained stone spring cup fixed to the right-side channel coping within reach of the water worker;
- one timber herb-drying frame with clearly hanging bundled nonmagical herbs directly under or immediately beside the market awning, used by the market/herb worker;
- one simple dark-timber guard weapon rest near the base of the existing large bell tower, holding a few plain maintained polearms but no guard figure.
Keep the ledger station, unreadable clay-name tablets, banked brazier, iron-bound rain barrels, rain chains, patched awning, and traveler bench. Tablet markings must remain entirely unreadable.

5. Preserve spring-versus-runoff separation. The warm spring continues downhill in its stone-lined channel and beneath the single stone arch. Roof rain remains captured by gutters, rain chains, barrels, and separate shallow drainage. Move the extreme-right rain chain/barrel slightly away from the spring edge if necessary so it cannot read as discharging into the drinking/service spring.

Absolutely no other change. No text, letters, numerals, readable marks, signs, labels, captions, maps, compass, arrows, route lines, diagram, inset, cutaway, split screen, UI, HUD, logo, watermark, presentation border, rune, insignia, monolith, statue, cathedral, castle, battlements, second plaza, second spring arch, lake, coast, cliffs, mountains, ocean, harbor, enemies, angels, demons, corpses, procession, combat, or supernatural spectacle.

